    <!--
        Who wrote this.

        A resource rather than a literal in the About screen, so it survives
        into `resources.arsc` and the manifest instead of only into compiled
        code. That is the difference between a name the app can draw and a name
        the *package* carries: anyone inspecting the APK — `aapt dump badging`,
        an app-info screen, a store listing tool — reads the manifest, and a
        string buried in classes.dex is invisible to all of them.

        The signing certificate cannot carry it. That key is fixed: its
        fingerprint is what the server publishes for App Link verification, and
        reissuing it would break every installed copy's update path.
    -->
    <string name="developer_name" translatable="false">Tahsin Faiyaz</string>
</resources>
